        "val": {
          "first": {
            "seq": 8,
            "text": "Install the notebooklm-skill from the GitHub repository https://github.com/claude-world/notebooklm-skill.git. The goal is to set up NotebookLM automation for terminals and AI agents. Follow the Quick start instructions: clone the repository, run ./install.sh, then run 'notebooklm-auth setup' and 'notebooklm-skill list'. Ensure ~/.local/bin is on PATH. The installer creates a dedicated virtual environment, installs Chromium, links five commands into ~/.local/bin, and installs the Claude Code Skill. Report back the outcome of each step, including any errors and their fixes. This is a Linux machine (Omarchy, Arch-based).\nYour parent agent id is \"session-00be52c7-0424-46c2-b104-b3e948156efe\". Before you finish, send your result to that agent with send_message({ agent_id: \"session-00be52c7-0424-46c2-b104-b3e948156efe\", message: \"<self-contained result>\" }). The parent shares your workspace but does not automatically receive your transcript, tool output, or reasoning. Send earlier messages as well when a finding changes what the parent should do next; sending a message does not end your turn."
          },
          "count": 1,
